cans/live-79829440?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Democratic Party gained control of the House and Senate, delivering a stinging rebuke to US President Donald Trump and his Republican Party. Follow DW's live updates.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>India news: Election body opens door for voter reinclusion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:58d8cd077bb3f3bc7b19894b62dee88039176407635a6626d822db6b3997f9fb</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:43:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T05:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-news-election-body-opens-door-for-voter-reinclusion/live-79849888--daa3a076e9e1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-news-election-body-opens-door-for-voter-reinclusion/live-79849888?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Indian poll body said no action will be taken against deleted voters for using Form 6 for re-enrolment in voter rolls. Follow DW for more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>From rotten food to political opponents: Researchers explore how disgust relates to our beliefs, and why the connection is complicated</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:da1aa0cf0843af6b8fcda592808e899282c1999c8386717a22dd3fc1e406970f</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T05:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/from-rotten-food-to-political-opponents-researchers-explore-how-disgust-relates-to-our-beliefs-and-w/a-79734659--e9b7cd7e436d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/from-rotten-food-to-political-opponents-researchers-explore-how-disgust-relates-to-our-beliefs-and-why-the-connection-is-complicated/a-79734659?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Some studies have linked disgust sensitivity to socially conservative attitudes. But does disgust shape our politics, or do our beliefs shape what we find disgusting?</summary><category term="Science" /></entry><entry><title>US to cut nearly $4 billion in Israel military aid, Trump says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85ad8266961759e9da7e5c5fa3faa5395d74a000e658260c0be105fd6b7fb5dd</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:43:56Z</updated><published>2026-11-04T00:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-to-cut-nearly-4-billion-in-israel-military-aid-trump-says/a-79848860--460a57fda36b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-to-cut-nearly-4-billion-in-israel-military-aid-trump-says/a-79848860?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">President Donald Trump said that the United States would still sell weapons to Israel. He added that Democratic candidates were using US military support for Israel against Republicans in the midterm elections.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Spain transport minister offers resignation in wake of train accident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4d48c92058b08d1702c2ecea1d237a748bbe6f9ef421cc20cfaa5292cd8d073</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spain-transport-minister-offers-resignation-in-wake-of-train-accident/a-79848097--3d039d9e0a30.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spain-transport-minister-offers-resignation-in-wake-of-train-accident/a-79848097?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">After two deadly train crashes this year, Spanish Transport Minister Oscar Puente has said he will step down.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Greenland's parliament ratifies Trump's US security agreement</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7152c571c78da44f934808e9fb10bc0d9c5120e5df7029f2627dcbbfac5073b2</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T20:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/greenland-s-parliament-ratifies-trump-s-us-security-agreement/a-79847399--1895871d284d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/greenland-s-parliament-ratifies-trump-s-us-security-agreement/a-79847399?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US is set to expand its military footprint on the Arctic island, part of the Kingdom of Denmark. It follows pressure from Donald Trump earlier in the year which opened a major rift in the transatlantic alliance.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK's King Charles III decries 'monstrous injustice' of slave trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bc4bd89a54d5ed57b981a612aec80e064edc1a95c73423de36fe6293dc628311</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T18:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-s-king-charles-iii-decries-monstrous-injustice-of-slave-trade/a-79845889--c33cef4229e5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-s-king-charles-iii-decries-monstrous-injustice-of-slave-trade/a-79845889?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">King Charles has told leaders at a Commonwealth summit that the legacy of the transatlantic slave trade "fills my heart with horror." He did not address calls for apologies and reparations.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Why South Africa's local elections matter</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cb43facfaba523f792e37bd15ea65dabe7faba1e4bd1b6688f94d0bf241c9391</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-south-africa-s-local-elections-matter/a-79842695--3bc8ee9505ed.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-south-africa-s-local-elections-matter/a-79842695?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">South Africans head to the polls on Wednesday amid water shortages, frustration with local services and questions over whether the ANC's support will keep falling.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine war: Merz doubts Russia is serious about a truce</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ead3702e38e1c55af2b80d90c2c64b8c08f14fe273e3f8ac3eb549f3c716eeeb</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T15:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-war-merz-doubts-russia-is-serious-about-a-truce/a-79836026--11d120b4fdbc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-war-merz-doubts-russia-is-serious-about-a-truce/a-79836026?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">German Chancellor Friedrich Merz met with Volodymyr Zelenskyy in Berlin. Both leaders said the EU needs to be included in peace talks with Russia. Merz also expressed doubts that Russia is serious about seeking a truce.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>China and India achieved diplomatic thaw. Now the border is flaring up</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8b251bb419c43d2d75c9c913ceb5c65dc578941339e74d8e329fe1bed08b75a4</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:48:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/china-and-india-achieved-diplomatic-thaw-now-the-border-is-flaring-up/a-79843273--6b47f2ce5be9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/china-and-india-achieved-diplomatic-thaw-now-the-border-is-flaring-up/a-79843273?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Indian authorities have confirmed a new border "face-off" between Indian and Chinese troops in Arunachal Pradesh, raising questions about the still fragile thaw in relations between New Delhi and Beijing.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>How Berlin's Arab queers are building their community</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6c6eda95742313984642b3470783f5577c3f7fd89e83a7fa9b0055c7eba2e81d</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143--c676c7f349f7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-berlin-s-arab-queers-are-building-their-community/a-79833143?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As the co-founder of the ADIRA Drag Festival, Lebanese performance artist, drag performer, DJ and cultural organizer Hassandra has become an essential part of Berlin's queer artistic landscape.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Cyprus: From ties with Russia to a strategic alignment with the US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c973cab1d5c5baa8bbdfa549a198f95d9f31a0dd9491c427d53feaf2576ad401</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/cyprus-from-ties-with-russia-to-a-strategic-alignment-with-the-us/a-79841251--5a66c266e064.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/cyprus-from-ties-with-russia-to-a-strategic-alignment-with-the-us/a-79841251?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Republic of Cyprus long balanced ties between Russia and the West. Now, it is phasing out Russian weapons, expanding defense cooperation with the United States and redefining its place in the Eastern Mediterranean.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>What US midterm elections mean for Ukraine, Iran and elsewhere</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:247c4de981635a1670ef930de1ce82321eb20ff65ae755935f2bc849c1132b7a</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-us-midterm-elections-mean-for-ukraine-iran-and-elsewhere/a-79836423--c94a74658887.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-us-midterm-elections-mean-for-ukraine-iran-and-elsewhere/a-79836423?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Donald Trump's Republicans control the US Congress, but that could change after the midterm elections. The outcome of the ballot will not only impact domestic policy but also conflicts in Europe and the Middle East.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen: Houthi clashes near Taiz leave residents in a 'state of panic'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2635f4bc98f1717f06d8fd61501858acd3af9bf473df9f0e09c77ee2482e6b71</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthi-clashes-near-taiz-leave-residents-in-a-state-of-panic/a-79836913--fbc4d150c8c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-houthi-clashes-near-taiz-leave-residents-in-a-state-of-panic/a-79836913?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fighting between Iran-backed Houthi rebels and Yemeni government forces has intensified around the city of Taiz. Residents face growing shortages of food, water and medical supplies as thousands flee their homes.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Multiple flights to European airports targeted by bomb threats</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8994ab4d2bafc7545894f20621282f0e0b4899509572b3086d5fb8fe11ce83ae</id><updated>2026-11-04T06:42:49Z</updated><published>2026-11-03T14:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/multiple-flights-to-european-airports-targeted-by-bomb-threats/a-79842434--863c4364baea.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/multiple-flights-to-european-airports-targeted-by-bomb-threats/a-79842434?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The bomb threats involved two passenger planes bound for Warsaw, a Ryanair flight from London to Spain, two flights to Rome and a flight traveling from Israe